values ('ap_calculus_ab', 3, '3.1', array['3.1', '3.2']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'Composite function: outer and inner functions', 'A composite function is a function embedded in another function; to differentiate it, decompose it into an outer function and an inner function, where y is a function of u and u is a function of x.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Common errors are misidentifying the inner function and forgetting to differentiate it. The chain rule also applies to sin²x, tan(2x − 1), and e^{x²}.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-calculus-ab-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_calculus_ab-u3-r1-003; ced=Building the Mathematical Practices: "decompose composite functions into their ''outer'' and ''inner'' component functions"')
